\begin_layout Section*
Significance for the practice
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The design of pavement structures is an extremely important task in the
 development and maintenance of transport infrastructure.
 A good design system helps the engineer to determine the required thickness
 and economic material composition of the pavement structure to withstand
 traffic and environmental loads over the lifetime of the road.
 In addition, a good pavement design system can also help to reduce environmenta
l impact, for example by minimizing material use and CO
\begin_inset script subscript

\begin_layout Plain Layout
2
\end_layout

\end_inset

 emissions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Taking into account the above aspects, the new scientific results presented
 in this thesis can be used to develop a new national design system that
 not only takes better account of the potential of material properties,
 but also allows for the development or comparison of more detailed technical
 alternatives to the currently used standard solutions.
 This is also an important task as pavement design systems and the associated
 technical standards and guidelines need to be updated from time to time
 to keep pace with technological developments and changing environmental
 challenges.
\end_layout

